WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.660
- 'Cause it's such an amazing thing for,

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.330
especially I was a young
girl and played soccer.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.730
Like that's a really cool thing to like,

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.455
watch a woman that you idolize.

00:00:07.455 --> 00:00:09.830
Like make it, and not just make it,

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.180
like bad ass kinda make it.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.083
- [Brandi] You know I think
to answer your question,

00:00:16.055 --> 00:00:17.460
It seems difficult.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.240
Like why would somebody
be upset about that?

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.980
But I think that the commentary
was they'd never seen

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.500
something like that before.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.330
And so that makes people
uncomfortable, right?

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.940
And so 99%, let's say 98% was like,

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.570
'Oh my gosh, this was the
greatest sporting event

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.430
I ever went to',

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.500
'I'm so happy that I
got to bring my kids.'

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.830
There's always gonna
be someone in your life

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.870
or some organization
that doesn't believe in

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.320
what you believe in,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.240
or see the things the
same way you see them.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.740
That's an opportunity to
bring people together.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.610
So for me it was like,
let's have a conversation.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:49.443
- Yeah.

00:00:49.443 --> 00:00:50.276
- [Brandi] You know, I did the interviews.

00:00:50.276 --> 00:00:53.015
You know, now my granddaughter
wants to take off her top

00:00:53.015 --> 00:00:56.520
and you know, you were sexualizing sports.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.353
I mean, Erin, look at her.

00:00:57.353 --> 00:00:58.620
She's heard the story already.
(laughs)

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.740
But this is what I said.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.573
Come out.

00:01:00.573 --> 00:01:01.406
See what we do.

00:01:01.406 --> 00:01:02.239
- [Erin] Yes.

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:03.072
- Give it a try.

00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:04.539
You'll understand what it's like.

00:01:04.539 --> 00:01:06.531
- And you're celebrating.
(audience clapping)

00:01:06.531 --> 00:01:08.313
Like it was amazing.

00:01:08.313 --> 00:01:10.910
- Listen, in '99 we
were responsible for the

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.229
future of women's soccer, right?

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:14.062
(laughs)

00:01:14.062 --> 00:01:17.800
And if we didn't win, it
would have all gone away.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.633
- Yeah.
- It would have been like,

00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:19.466
'Oh that was cute.'
- You did.

00:01:19.466 --> 00:01:20.299
- 'That was sweet.'
- [Erin] Right.

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:22.180
- You ignited the domino
effect with change.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.649
- [Brandi] Yeah, and instead,
you know, that team took on

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:28.776
all that responsibility and
understood how to filter that,

00:01:28.776 --> 00:01:33.776
and to do what they do, how
to do, at the right time

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.770
and be ready to be champions.

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:36.603
- Yeah.

00:01:36.603 --> 00:01:38.970
- That is not easy to do but
they did it at the right time.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.880
- [Kelly] Hard work. Hard work pays off.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.390
- In my opinion, hard work
should be a common denominator.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:45.590
We all should work hard.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:46.907
That's, you know, you got that.

00:01:46.907 --> 00:01:47.870
- [Kelly] But we all don't.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.610
And that's why only some of
us are champions. (laughs)

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:50.443
- Yeah.

